## Avoiding Unnecessary Re-renders

{% if variables.state_library == 'Zustand' %}
### Fine-Grained Zustand Selectors

Subscribe to specific values, not the entire store.

```typescript
// CORRECT - Only re-renders when filterCategory changes
const filterCategory = useTransactionStore((s) => s.filterCategory);

// WRONG - Re-renders on ANY store change
const { filterCategory } = useTransactionStore();
```

{% elif variables.state_library == 'Redux Toolkit' %}
### Narrow Redux Selectors

Select single values with `useAppSelector`; derive with `createSelector` so a new
array/object is not returned on every call.

```typescript
// CORRECT
const filterCategory = useAppSelector((s) => s.transactionFilter.category);

// WRONG - returns a new object every time -> re-render on any state change
const { category, sort } = useAppSelector((s) => ({ ...s.transactionFilter }));
```

{% elif variables.state_library == 'MobX' %}
### MobX Observers

Wrap every component that reads observables in `observer`, and dereference
observables as late as possible (in the child that displays them).

```typescript
// CORRECT - only FilterLabel re-renders when the filter changes
const FilterLabel = observer(function FilterLabel() {
  return <Text>{filterStore.category}</Text>;
});
```

{% elif variables.state_library == 'Jotai' %}
### Small Jotai Atoms

One atom per value; derived atoms for computed values. A component re-renders only
for the atoms it reads, so don't bundle unrelated values into one object atom.

```typescript
// CORRECT
export const filterCategoryAtom = atom<string | null>(null);
const category = useAtomValue(filterCategoryAtom);
```

{% endif %}
### Stable References Outside React

The compiler memoizes values inside components, but not values passed to effects in
non-compiled code or module-level caches. Keep constants at module scope.

```typescript
const EMPTY_ITEMS: Item[] = [];   // module scope
const items = data ?? EMPTY_ITEMS;
```

### Split Components

Split large components into smaller ones so that state changes only re-render
the relevant portion.

```typescript
// CORRECT - Filter bar re-renders independently of the list
function ItemsScreen() {
  return (
    <View>
      <FilterBar />  {/* Owns its filter state */}
      <ItemList />   {/* Has its own query subscription */}
    </View>
  );
}

// WRONG - Entire screen re-renders when filter changes
function ItemsScreen() {
  const [filter, setFilter] = useState(defaultFilter); // every keystroke re-renders the list
  const { data } = useItems(filter);
  return (
    <View>
      <FilterBar filter={filter} onChange={setFilter} />
      <FlashList data={data} ... />
    </View>
  );
}
```

